{"name":"Britches","hex":"#a09073","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"britches","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of breeches (pants, trousers).","The roe of cod."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/britches"}],"entries":[{"title":"Breeches","blocks":[{"text":"Breeches or britches are an article of clothing covering the body from the waist down, with separate coverings for each leg, usually stopping just below the knee, though in some cases reaching to the ankles. Formerly a standard item of Western men's clothing, they had fallen out of use by the mid-19th century in favour of trousers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Elijah_Boardman_MET_DT60.jpg/330px-Elijah_Boardman_MET_DT60.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breeches","wikidata":"Q2302770"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Koninklijk_Koetsier_2013_74.JPG/500px-Koninklijk_Koetsier_2013_74.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Koninklijk_Koetsier_2013_74.JPG/500px-Koninklijk_Koetsier_2013_74.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Breeches are still worn as livery for special occasions in several European courts. Here, a coachman in the Netherlands wears them during Prinsjesdag, 2013.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKoninklijk_Koetsier_2013_74.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Elijah_Boardman_MET_DT60.jpg/500px-Elijah_Boardman_MET_DT60.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Elijah_Boardman_MET_DT60.jpg/500px-Elijah_Boardman_MET_DT60.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conte